    "granted_by": "Maintainer decision, 2026-08-23. 'GO for Recovery Continuation Attempt 7. I reviewed the tokenizer repair. 30dcee3 is the tested implementation that produced 2183 passed / 12 skipped and continuation harness b824441c; 9ca708a is only the state follow-up pointing baseline_commit at that tested tree, so it does not alter the executable harness. The repair preserves the frozen evaluation protocol correctly. After training, materialize_eval_tokenizer() copies exactly tokenizer.json, tokenizer_config.json and chat_template.jinja from the already-attested CANONICAL_INIT into the trained model directory, with missing-source and conflicting-destination cases failing closed and byte equality reverified. battery() remains unchanged and must continue passing only --model <trained model dir>, with no --tokenizer. Therefore the material tokenizer-source rule remains \"the evaluated checkpoint\". The existing post-generation RecoveryEvaluationProtocol.require_comparable() remains the authoritative paid-path check that the resulting tokenizer/template/runtime identity actually matches the frozen Stage-3 protocol. Do not change Stage-1 artifact identity or recovery science merely because the evaluation view of the newly trained checkpoint now contains the frozen tokenizer sidecars.' Against last tested implementation 30dcee3, with 9ca708a as the state follow-up. Since attempt 6 one closure landed and was accepted: THE EVALUATION TOKENIZER. Attempt 6 trained a rung-1 probe for 71.9 minutes, resolved its checkpoint through the repaired trained_model_dir(), entered battery() -- past the line that ended attempt 5 -- and then died on apply_chat_template because Trainer.save_checkpoint writes weights and config only, so the checkpoint carried no tokenizer, and uncapped_eval's --tokenizer defaults to the checkpoint's own. Passing --tokenizer was REJECTED as a protocol change: tokenizer_source is material under generation_runtime_comparability@v2 and Stage 0 attests \"the evaluated checkpoint\", so an external source would make every probe incomparable to the Stage-3 controls that materialized the equivalence interval and feasibility floor. The frozen rule is instead made true by materializing the attested bytes into the evaluated checkpoint. uncapped_eval.py was deliberately untouched because it is part of the generation source digest. Verified on the current tree: full suite 2183 passed / 12 skipped, +7 with the skip count unchanged; frozen-asset verifier passed with no problems; 5 mutations each turning a passing state into a failing one, including a 5-minute end-to-end run proving the stage-1-5 harness catches a removed materialization. The continuation harness digest moved 8b56fc7b -> b824441c.\n\nCovers: One (1) launch of the AutoInitializer Phase-A RECOVERY CONTINUATION, attempt 7, on a single NVIDIA L40S at no more than $0.99/h. It imports the verified Attempt-12 Stage-1 result -- the five preserved selected leaves, in the committed selected order, re-identified from the bytes that actually arrive on the pod -- and runs recovery Stages 2 through 5 under the frozen science, the existing watchdog, soft-stop, hard-stop, artifact-gate and provider-confirmed teardown behaviour. Everything ahead of the battery is already demonstrated on paid hardware and is not revisited: the transport (attempts 3-4), Stage 0 and the strict Stage-1 import with control measurement and admission (attempts 4-6), the release and headroom contracts (attempt 5), and the probe checkpoint resolution (attempt 6). Attempts 5 and 6 each trained one rung-1 probe and lost it with its pod; neither is resumable scientific work, so this attempt starts recovery normally from the preserved Stage-1 inputs and retrains. Authorized pricing is DERIVED from continuation_budget(), not written: expected $14.9233, per-launch hard ceiling $16.7456, which is also the hard cap. The beam search is not run, not reconstructed, and is structurally unreachable from this harness.\n\nCumulative spend at approval $217.1763 against a cumulative cap of $234.00.\n\nDoes NOT authorize: Increasing the cumulative cap, the per-launch ceiling, or any live-run budget extension; overriding, deferring or reinterpreting a soft-stop or hard-stop refusal. Changing Stage-1 artifact identity or recovery science because the evaluation view of a newly trained checkpoint now contains the frozen tokenizer sidecars. Passing --tokenizer to uncapped_eval.py, or otherwise altering the material tokenizer-source rule, the generation source digest, generation comparability v2, the Stage-3 attestation or any frozen threshold or protocol identity. Editing uncapped_eval.py, the trainer, Trainer.save_checkpoint or the frozen recovery recipe. Trained-but-unscored resume or retention machinery. New canaries, new harness layers, Stage-1 work, transport work, or memory recalibration. Rerunning or redesigning Stage 1; a beam search or any reconstruction of the search. Re-ranking or re-selecting the five leaves or changing their committed order. Retraining the permanent controls. Measuring the canonical control more than once or on anything but the frozen Stage-1 suite. Repairing and relaunching on a live pod. Any follow-on or automatically started session. Reusing any spent grant or authorization from attempts 1 through 6. Any other paid session.\n\nGrant document: logs/autoinit_recovery_continuation_attempt7_grant.json sha256 4398501f5ff0e90397d45f890c1782b56b316e913f81b68228850220b44fd5a8",
